 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:15:02.591809Z",
 "text": "Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* (RTA), security of tenure is a fundamental principle. A residential tenancy cannot be terminated automatically by a contingency, condition, or event stipulated in a lease agreement. \n\nSection 37(1) of the RTA establishes that a tenancy may be terminated **only** in accordance with the Act (such as through prescribed statutory notices, an application to the Landlord and Tenant Board, or a valid agreement to terminate made after the tenancy has begun). Because taking a job outside Ontario is not a recognized lawful ground for termination under the Act, the clause attempts to contract out of the statutory termination scheme and is of no force or effect (and is void under section 4).\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 37",
